## 12 GENERAL SAFETY REQUIREMENTS

In order to reduce the accidents during transportation, the various stakeholders should ensure the following:

- a) Never overload the vehicle beyond its carrying capacity;
- b) Before starting the vehicle, transport agency/agent should ensure that the material loaded on the vehicle is properly stowed, lashed and secured;




- c) Consignor, if desired, may also inspect the loaded cargo to ensure that the consignment is adequately secured to meet the required standards;
- d) Never drive the vehicle beyond the speed limit;
- e) Never sit or take rest under the vehicle or within the vicinity of 10 feet of the vehicle or at any parking place area;
- f) Use seat belt while driving vehicle and all the vehicles should be fitted with seat belt for all the crew member(s), if allowed;
- g) Any crewmember including helper should not distract/disturb the driver while driving the vehicle;
- h) Date and time of duty start of the driver should be recorded in a logbook so as to monitor duty stipulated hours;
- j) No illegal person should be allowed to travel in the vehicle. Seating capacity should be as per the registration certificate of the vehicle;
- k) Trainings of crew members including first aid use should be ensured;
- m) Should not use mobile phones while
driving, with or without accessories like hands free, wireless, headset and bluetooth etc; and

- n) Vehicle servicing and maintenance should
